  "name": "Chanzuns rumantschas (Romansh folk and choral song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song in Romansh, the Rhaeto-Romance language of Graubünden, from Engadine (Ladin) folk songs and the Chalandamarz songs that children sing on 1 March with cowbells to drive out the winter, to the village men's and mixed choirs that carry much of the repertoire today. As early as 1912-15 the Engadine poet Peider Lansel recorded Ladin folk songs on a phonograph, and the folklorist Alfons Maissen later collected Romansh folk song.",
  "recipe": "classic early-1910s chanzuns rumantschas, ballad Poetry. mixed satb canonical 4 part western global traditional polyphonic choir ensemble. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
